{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm","id":1508391,"title":"If Wraiths are just memories, wouldn't they fit better in the Astral Realm?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-14T14:15:47-07:00","id":1508391,"title":"If Wraiths are just memories, wouldn't they fit better in the Astral Realm?","content":"The wiki states that Wraiths and the Shadowlands are really just memories. If this is true wouldnt it be more fitting for both Wraiths and the Shadowlands to be found in the Astral Realm instead of the Underworld? It feels more fitting to have actual Souls inhabit the Underworld than the remnant memories of individuals long gone and not be affected or altered by the memories of the living or dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 04-14-2023, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T14:39:16-07:00","id":1508393,"title":"","content":"If you do that, what would you put in the Underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T14:52:15-07:00","id":1508395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm?p=1508393#post1508393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do that, what would you put in the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actual souls I guess? Maybe do what DA:M did by having multiple different afterlives, heavens, and hells within the underworld. Maybe have the Greek afterlife neighbouring the Norse afterlife. <br /> <br /> IMO, this is a lot more interesting compared to the way the Underworld is structured currently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 04-14-2023, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T15:28:22-07:00","id":1508396,"title":"","content":"&quot;According to the wiki&quot; isn't really a compelling thing here. Whether or not wraiths are the souls of dead humans, they are full spiritual entities of a specific nature. They're not &quot;just memories&quot; because they can and will do things.<br /> <br /> It's officially the case that you can run into both Underworld and Astral versions of the same person as it is. It's also officially the case that even in the modern era, the Underworld shifts according to dominant beliefs and that while more homogeneous now than it used to be, there are distinct areas of it that work differently as dictated by human input.Stygia is not the only option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T05:53:35-07:00","id":1508433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm?p=1508395#post1508395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actual souls I guess? Maybe do what DA:M did by having multiple different afterlives, heavens, and hells within the underworld. Maybe have the Greek afterlife neighbouring the Norse afterlife.<br /> <br /> IMO, this is a lot more interesting compared to the way the Underworld is structured currently.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Soul' isn't a well-defined concept. The definition depends on culture and personal philosophy. I could say that every living human being is the sum of their memories, their actions and decisions the causal consequence of them, and their soul the emergent property thereof. Memories running on a meat platform. A lot of transhumanist thought hinges on that concept, for example.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a religious person would probably very much disagree with that definition, and for twenty different religions you would get twenty different definitions of the soul. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, the underworld provides different 'regions' that cater to these different philosophies (cf. <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Kingdom\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Kingdoms</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Far_Shore\" target=\"_blank\">Far Shores</a>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T06:43:40-07:00","id":1508436,"title":"","content":"The Astral/High Umbra is the realm of higher thought. While the Dark/Low Umbra is the layer of memory, of what was. So ghosts are exactly where they need to be.<br /> Though iconic characters will undoubtedly have a High Umbra representation as well. Saints, Robin Hood, Elvis... These are more than just memories to humanity at large, they're mentally kept alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T09:50:33-07:00","id":1508457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm#post1508391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wiki states that Wraiths and the Shadowlands are really just memories. If this is true wouldnt it be more fitting for both Wraiths and the Shadowlands to be found in the Astral Realm instead of the Underworld? It feels more fitting to have actual Souls inhabit the Underworld than the remnant memories of individuals long gone and not be affected or altered by the memories of the living or dead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the whute wolf wiki is full of things not backed up by books or stating as facts what some books state as opinions from specific narrators.<br /> <br /> As far as wraith the oblivion and most other supernatural are concerned, wraiths are actually the souls of the restless dead.<br /> <br /> Howether, the environnement and the corpus of wraith is made of memories, which may be (let's be charitable) what the wiki is refering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T09:54:14-07:00","id":1508458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm?p=1508433#post1508433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'Soul' isn't a well-defined concept. The definition depends on culture and personal philosophy. I could say that every living human being is the sum of their memories, their actions and decisions the causal consequence of them, and their soul the emergent property thereof. Memories running on a meat platform. A lot of transhumanist thought hinges on that concept, for example.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a religious person would probably very much disagree with that definition, and for twenty different religions you would get twenty different definitions of the soul. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, the underworld provides different 'regions' that cater to these different philosophies (cf. <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Kingdom\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Kingdoms</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Far_Shore\" target=\"_blank\">Far Shores</a>).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> to be fair, &quot;soul&quot; is a pretty specific and narrow concept. It's consciousness. The &quot;I&quot; in I am. And it is an immaterial thing. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T12:00:48-07:00","id":1508470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm?p=1508458#post1508458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">to be fair, &quot;soul&quot; is a pretty specific and narrow concept. It's consciousness. The &quot;I&quot; in I am. And it is an immaterial thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Then what about the subconscious mind?.<br /> <br /> *If only the experience of consciousness it's &quot;the I in I am&quot;, do you stop having a soul when unconscious?.<br /> <br /> It's said that in deep states of meditation one can suspend consciousness entirely. I was told this was a big problem for Budhissts, because their philosophy struggles to explain how can consciousness &quot;resume&quot; after being suspended, if there's no &quot;self&quot; to restart it...Implying that the notion should be deeper than consciousness not just for Buddhists, but also for some of their <i>detractors</i>?<br /> <br /> The <i>*I* in I am</i><i>.</i>..one could also say it's merely a way to conceptualize the chest beating used to signal &quot;me&quot;. That, actually, signals more towards the body than to &quot;the consciousness&quot;. The &quot;body&quot; being a pretty good candidate for *I*, if you believe your biology, or at least your brain, have things to say about that *I* , that the *I* may not even be aware off but are still part of it.<br /> <br /> Then again, if there's something that can't be &quot;the soul&quot;, it's &quot;the body&quot;. Rigth?. Well, ancient egyptians said it was a part of it...so Wraiths could actually be *part* of a soul, a soul that actually exists in several other places and some parts of it can perish? (I think this jives <i>decently </i>well with WoD cosmology, actually, not that this is &quot;the truth&quot;. Well, it kinda seems to be in Mummy. To say something positive about it for Mage/Wraith: It could be one way to conciliate the &quot;Wraith-as-soul&quot; and the &quot;Avatar-as-Soul&quot;, maybe they're different &quot;parts&quot; of the soul that get detached on death)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-15-2023, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T18:35:38-07:00","id":1508501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm?p=1508470#post1508470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Then what about the subconscious mind?.<br /> <br /> *If only the experience of consciousness it's &quot;the I in I am&quot;, do you stop having a soul when unconscious?.<br /> <br /> It's said that in deep states of meditation one can suspend consciousness entirely. I was told this was a big problem for Budhissts, because their philosophy struggles to explain how can consciousness &quot;resume&quot; after being suspended, if there's no &quot;self&quot; to restart it...Implying that the notion should be deeper than consciousness not just for Buddhists, but also for some of their <i>detractors</i>?<br /> <br /> The <i>*I* in I am</i><i>.</i>..one could also say it's merely a way to conceptualize the chest beating used to signal &quot;me&quot;. That, actually, signals more towards the body than to &quot;the consciousness&quot;. The &quot;body&quot; being a pretty good candidate for *I*, if you believe your biology, or at least your brain, have things to say about that *I* , that the *I* may not even be aware off but are still part of it.<br /> <br /> Then again, if there's something that can't be &quot;the soul&quot;, it's &quot;the body&quot;. Rigth?. Well, ancient egyptians said it was a part of it...so Wraiths could actually be *part* of a soul, a soul that actually exists in several other places and some parts of it can perish? (I think this jives <i>decently </i>well with WoD cosmology, actually, not that this is &quot;the truth&quot;. Well, it kinda seems to be in Mummy. To say something positive about it for Mage/Wraith: It could be one way to conciliate the &quot;Wraith-as-soul&quot; and the &quot;Avatar-as-Soul&quot;, maybe they're different &quot;parts&quot; of the soul that get detached on death)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In a soul or more precisely a dualistic model of consciousness, the subconscious mind is part of consciousness, and being &quot;unconscious&quot; is irrelevant, since it's merely basically sleeping period.<br /> the body, in a dualist model, is merely the vessel of the soul, so it is unrelated to the soul.<br /> <br /> These interesting issues that you bring are important when you use a materialist, or emergent view of consciousness, which is hence based on brain functions and states, hence dependant on it's relation to the rest of the body, it's relation to being unconscious and having inner working that we call subconscious.<br /> Dualists don't entertain these ideas for it does not matter on the nature of a soul<br /> <br /> And to be precise about egyptian anatomy of the soul, as far as we know, they didn't consider the body as part of the soul, they consider it a part of a living human, and it was a natural part of one's life to let it behind when death comes<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 04-15-2023, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T06:40:15-07:00","id":1508628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm?p=1508470#post1508470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then again, if there's something that can't be &quot;the soul&quot;, it's &quot;the body&quot;. Rigth?. Well, ancient egyptians said it was a part of it...so Wraiths could actually be *part* of a soul, a soul that actually exists in several other places and some parts of it can perish? (I think this jives <i>decently </i>well with WoD cosmology, actually, not that this is &quot;the truth&quot;. Well, it kinda seems to be in Mummy. To say something positive about it for Mage/Wraith: It could be one way to conciliate the &quot;Wraith-as-soul&quot; and the &quot;Avatar-as-Soul&quot;, maybe they're different &quot;parts&quot; of the soul that get detached on death)</div> </div> </div> </div>My preferred way of looking at things is that the Wraith is the manifestation of the parts of a person that are unwilling to let go of the world. More specifically, the Psyche is the presentation of the parts that refuse to let go of the world and the Shadow is the presentation of the parts that want to end entirely. Under this model, the Avatar, Eidolon, and the rest of the person are all chilling at the edge of Transcendence waiting to see if the Psyche and Shadow will get their act together or if they will be scraped off on the edge of Oblivion. <br /> <br /> This is headcanon, of course, but it does help me explain how the Avatar can be part of the soul and at the same time not at risk of Oblivion. It also means the Chakravanti are not callous idiots for thinking sending wraiths to Oblivion is helping them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T21:06:04-07:00","id":1508708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm#post1508391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wiki states that Wraiths and the Shadowlands are really just memories. If this is true wouldnt it be more fitting for both Wraiths and the Shadowlands to be found in the Astral Realm instead of the Underworld? It feels more fitting to have actual Souls inhabit the Underworld than the remnant memories of individuals long gone and not be affected or altered by the memories of the living or dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what gameline you're running. Kindred of the East (and the 1000 Hells sourcebook) takes the position that Wraiths are very much souls, not memories, and that the Underworld is a place that souls go to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T05:25:36-07:00","id":1508738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm?p=1508708#post1508708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on what gameline you're running. Kindred of the East (and the 1000 Hells sourcebook) takes the position that Wraiths are very much souls, not memories, and that the Underworld is a place that souls go to.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also counter to a lot of what Wraith has to say about people being stuck by their own burdens and that there is a possibility to move onwards from the Underworld if you manage to lose the baggage of your life that's shackling you into the existence of a Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T06:03:14-07:00","id":1508740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm?p=1508738#post1508738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also counter to a lot of what Wraith has to say about people being stuck by their own burdens and that there is a possibility to move onwards from the Underworld if you manage to lose the baggage of your life that's shackling you into the existence of a Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Most of the process of your Dharma involves coming to grips with your existence as one of the undead and moving past it once you get to 10 dots. That's why staying at 9 dots nets you the title of boddhisattva (sufficiently enlightened, but sticking behind to help others find the way), and why some of the high-Dharma folks who knew the three that took on Zapathasura simply just faded out when delivered news of their demise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T06:34:30-07:00","id":1508744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508391-if-wraiths-are-just-memories-wouldn-t-they-fit-better-in-the-astral-realm?p=1508740#post1508740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily. Most of the process of your Dharma involves coming to grips with your existence as one of the undead and moving past it once you get to 10 dots. That's why staying at 9 dots nets you the title of boddhisattva (sufficiently enlightened, but sticking behind to help others find the way), and why some of the high-Dharma folks who knew the three that took on Zapathasura simply just faded out when delivered news of their demise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was agreeing with Anubis and giving corraborating evidence for that from Wraith itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_